---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../../config/site';
---

<ArticleLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  metaTitle={`Terms of Use | ${siteConfig.name}`}
  metaDescription={`Read the Terms of Use governing your access to ${siteConfig.name} home improvement calculators, cost guides, and estimation tools.`}
  pathname="/terms/"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Terms of Use', href: '/terms/' }]}
>
  <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-muted">
    Last Updated: <strong class="text-ink">{siteConfig.lastUpdatedDefault}</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    By accessing and using <strong>{siteConfig.name}</strong> ({siteConfig.url}), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Use and our <a href="/disclaimer/" class="text-blueprint underline">Construction Disclaimer</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mt-6">
    1. Permitted Personal &amp; Commercial Estimating Use
  </h2>
  <p>
    You may freely use our calculators, print project worksheets, and share calculation URLs for your personal DIY projects or residential contracting estimates. You may not scrape, republish, or frame our source code or calculator datasets on competing websites without written permission from {siteConfig.legalName}.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mt-6">
    2. No Structural Engineering or Legal Warranty
  </h2>
  <p>
    All calculators, formulas, and cost ranges on {siteConfig.name} are provided "AS IS" without warranty of any kind, express or implied. Building codes, frost-line depths, soil bearing capacities, structural loads, and material coverage rates vary by jurisdiction and substrate. Always verify structural designs and local code compliance with your municipal building department or a licensed professional engineer.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink mt-6">
    3. Limitation of Liability
  </h2>
  <p>
    Under no circumstances shall {siteConfig.legalName}, its editors, or contributors be liable for any material overages, shortages, property damage, or financial loss resulting from reliance on estimates generated by this website.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
